The definition of {konju} is rather cryptic.

x1 is a cone [shape/form] of material x2 with vertex x3. Also ellipse,
ellipsoid (= konclupa). See also jesni, djine, sovda, kojna, jganu.

"Cone" is this object: https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/File:PovCone.jpg
either only the surface of an object made after the revolution of a
triangle. That's why konju3 seems strange. Why only vertex is defined?

Definitely cone it's not an ellipse.

Could you please explain this?

